WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.702
Good morning, listeners.

2
00:00:03.652 --> 00:00:07.488
Today is September 29, 2026.

3
00:00:07.488 --> 00:00:11.839
Overnight, Wall Street closed lower in choppy consolidation.

4
00:00:11.839 --> 00:00:18.089
The S and P 500 slipped fifty-nine points, down zero point seven seven percent.

5
00:00:18.089 --> 00:00:23.763
The Nasdaq shed two hundred forty-eight points, down zero point nine two percent.

6
00:00:23.763 --> 00:00:28.983
Key indices remain trapped between their five-day and ten-day moving averages.

7
00:00:28.983 --> 00:00:32.929
Global sovereign debt markets flashed red alerts overnight.

8
00:00:32.929 --> 00:00:37.672
The thirty-year Treasury yield climbed to five point five five percent.

9
00:00:37.672 --> 00:00:42.574
All benchmarks beyond five years now sit firmly above five percent.

10
00:00:42.574 --> 00:00:46.925
Bond volatility spiked at its fastest clip in over a year.

11
00:00:46.925 --> 00:00:55.282
Apollo warns artificial intelligence agents are accelerating deposit flight into high-yield accounts, prolonging structural high interest rates.

12
00:00:55.282 --> 00:01:00.429
Meanwhile, federal funds rate expectations face a massive divergence.

13
00:01:00.429 --> 00:01:06.312
The CME FedWatch tool prices a seventy percent probability of an October rate hike.

14
00:01:06.312 --> 00:01:13.554
Federal Reserve Governor Cook flagged energy and infrastructure demands from data centers as immediate inflation drivers.

15
00:01:13.554 --> 00:01:19.780
Goldman Sachs warns rate cuts are over-priced, projecting one additional hike before any pause.

16
00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:28.836
Conversely, Treasury Secretary Bessent argues artificial intelligence productivity gains will ultimately crush inflation and lower long-term yields.

17
00:01:28.836 --> 00:01:32.709
Geopolitical risks offered marginal relief overnight.

18
00:01:32.709 --> 00:01:40.331
Saudi Arabia restarted its East-West pipeline, restoring seven million barrels per day bypassing the Strait of Hormuz.

19
00:01:40.331 --> 00:01:45.086
Middle East exports rebounded to twelve point eight million barrels per day.

20
00:01:45.086 --> 00:01:52.170
Brent crude trades cautiously around one hundred five dollars per barrel on pending Washington-Tehran negotiations.

21
00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:57.795
Liquidity tightening has raised the return hurdle on enterprise artificial intelligence spending.

22
00:01:57.795 --> 00:02:03.640
Bank of America warns institutional leverage metrics are nearing critical de-risking thresholds.

23
00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:07.574
Yet tech giants continue aggressive capital deployment.

24
00:02:07.574 --> 00:02:14.510
Meta launched its full-stack Enterprise Platform, triggering a twenty-five percent plunge in MongoDB shares.

25
00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:21.949
OpenAI is preparing its always-on Ode assistant alongside a five-hundred-dollar monthly GPT Pro Max tier.

26
00:02:21.949 --> 00:02:28.714
In cybersecurity, CrowdStrike, ticker C-R-W-D, pushed higher within an ascending channel.

27
00:02:28.714 --> 00:02:36.349
Broad sector exposure through the C-I-B-R and B-U-G exchange traded funds continues attracting defensive inflows.

28
00:02:36.349 --> 00:02:39.290
Now to our pivotal equities of the day.

29
00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:46.925
Nvidia, ticker N-V-D-A, closed at two hundred twenty-eight dollars with a market cap surpassing five trillion dollars.

30
00:02:46.925 --> 00:02:52.255
Management approved a historic one-hundred-fifty-billion-dollar share buyback program.

31
00:02:52.255 --> 00:02:59.081
That brings total authorized repurchases to two hundred thirty-five billion dollars through January 2028.

32
00:02:59.081 --> 00:03:04.461
Anthropic also secured a one-hundred-eighty-billion-dollar long-term compute agreement.

33
00:03:04.461 --> 00:03:12.023
Nvidia also unveiled a real-time, two-tier artificial intelligence safety system for agent runtime isolation.

34
00:03:12.023 --> 00:03:20.086
The thesis remains intact, but elevated valuation multiples leave limited upside at current levels without broader market breakout.

35
00:03:20.086 --> 00:03:26.189
Tesla, ticker T-S-L-A, faces rising delivery headwinds ahead of third-quarter numbers.

36
00:03:26.189 --> 00:03:30.601
JPMorgan cut its price target to four hundred fifteen dollars.

37
00:03:30.601 --> 00:03:38.003
Wall Street consensus stands at four hundred seventy thousand units, down from four hundred ninety-seven thousand last year.

38
00:03:38.003 --> 00:03:45.699
With Optimus and Robotaxi volume still quarters away, a ten percent year-over-year drop could trigger concentrated liquidation.

39
00:03:45.699 --> 00:03:51.336
Micron Technology, ticker M-U, reports fiscal fourth-quarter earnings tomorrow.

40
00:03:51.336 --> 00:03:59.902
Consensus targets fifty-one point two billion dollars in revenue, up thirty-five percent, and thirty-six billion dollars in net income.

41
00:03:59.902 --> 00:04:05.687
Dynamic random access memory blended average selling prices surged over sixty percent.

42
00:04:05.687 --> 00:04:13.432
Bulls point to one hundred billion dollars in long-term capacity agreements through 2030 and tight high-bandwidth memory supply.

43
00:04:13.432 --> 00:04:20.393
Bears, led by Michael Burry, warn memory pricing is peaking ahead of 2028 capacity expansions.

44
00:04:20.393 --> 00:04:25.552
Management forward guidance on enterprise high-bandwidth memory will dictate the trade.

45
00:04:25.688 --> 00:04:33.248
SpaceX tracked orbital success on its fourteenth Starship test flight, deploying Starlink V-3 satellites.

46
00:04:33.198 --> 00:04:40.820
SPCX traded flat after initial pops, as institutional desks await sustained commercial revenue conversion.

47
00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:48.259
Watch the forty-seven hundred support zone on the S and P, and maintain strict stop losses across high-beta names.

48
00:04:48.259 --> 00:04:52.266
That concludes today's XiaoFang Finance Morning Brief.

49
00:04:52.266 --> 00:04:56.433
Thank you for listening, trade safely, and see you tomorrow.
